- differential group/granular tests and generated pass docs

## ALGORITHM

1. Represent the seven contributor-facing groups as scheduling nodes that contain ordinary granular `PassConfig` children, not functions that privately loop over them.
2. Execute every child through one runner so stable ID, timing, diagnostics, result transition, snapshots, and later legality/invalidation hooks see the actual pass.
3. Preserve the exact 578-pass order, group boundaries, phase/scope assignments, and enabled/disabled behavior from the frozen registry baseline.
4. Initially preserve today's group-level capability snapshot semantics; changing capability invalidation/recomputation belongs to the following analysis task.
5. Run the opaque and transparent runners differentially over complete generated file trees, pass-selection counts, diagnostics, and bounded profiles.
6. Remove the opaque runner only after default grouped execution and explicit granular execution are byte-identical and report the same inner work.

## FAILURE MODES

- recomputing capabilities at a new cadence in the same change and altering pass eligibility;
- flattening away useful human-readable groups;
- hiding inner failures or returning a group-level success after a child failure;
- changing result-invariant enforcement rather than only improving first-pass attribution;
- changing pass order, scope, or output;
- unacceptable compile-time growth from debug hooks enabled in normal builds.

## TESTS

- opaque-versus-transparent complete tree parity during migration;
- group membership and inner pass count/order assertions;
- exact inner pass attribution for result-invariant mutation and synthetic pass failure;
- capability snapshot compatibility;
- timing/snapshot records for inner passes;
- bounded compile-time and memory comparisons;
- scoped/all-pass and source/package parity.

