## ALGORITHM

1. Add a closed node such as `EInterpolatedString(Array<EInterpolationPart>)`, where each part is literal text or a child ElixirAST expression carrying metadata/source position.
2. Flatten `StringConcat` chains left-to-right, merge adjacent literal parts, and preserve literal data without embedding target delimiters.
3. Apply required expression legalization structurally; remove redundant source `toString` only under the existing proven interpolation contract.
4. Teach the canonical mapper/traverser, equality helpers, use/scope analyzers, rewriters, metadata propagation, and debug snapshots to visit expression parts.
5. Make the printer solely responsible for quotes, literal escaping, literal `#{`, and rendering `#{child}` with correct precedence.
6. Migrate consumers that scan ERaw/EString interpolation text to structural traversal. Keep scanners only for explicit raw-authority inputs and name that authority.
7. Treat the new interpolation form as a structural ElixirAST node, not a separate semantic plan. If a later boundary requires another structural target form, lower it through one owned transform; never convert it back to ERaw internally.

