- double escaping or changing runtime bytes;
- reordering or duplicating embedded expression evaluation;
- losing throws/side effects, source positions, or metadata;
- wrapping every interpolation in an unnecessary IIFE;
- retaining text scanners for compiler-owned structural strings;
- treating arbitrary `#{` in an ordinary Haxe string as target code;
- allowing raw injection to masquerade as a structural interpolated string;
- snapshot-only proof without BEAM runtime assertions.

